      "question": "The curve has equation y = x^3/6 + 4 sqrt(x) - 15, x >= 0. Find dy/dx in simplest form.",
      "status": "ready",
      "answer": "dy/dx = x^2/2 + 2/sqrt(x)",
      "steps": [
        "Write each term as a power: y = (1/6)x^3 + 4x^(1/2) - 15.",
        "Use d/dx(x^n) = n x^(n-1) on each term.",
        "(1/6)x^3 gives (1/2)x^2.",
        "4x^(1/2) gives 2x^(-1/2) = 2/sqrt(x).",
        "The constant -15 differentiates to 0, so dy/dx = x^2/2 + 2/sqrt(x)."
      ]
    },
