      "question": "The point P(4, 11/3) lies on the curve in Q1(a). Find the equation of the normal to the curve at P in the form ax + by + c = 0, where a, b, c are integers.",
      "status": "ready",
      "answer": "x + 9y - 37 = 0",
      "steps": [
        "At x = 4: dy/dx = 16/2 + 2/2 = 9, the tangent gradient.",
        "Normal gradient = -1/9 (negative reciprocal).",
        "Use y - 11/3 = -1/9 (x - 4).",
        "Multiply by 9: 9y - 33 = -x + 4.",
        "Rearrange: x + 9y - 37 = 0.",
        "Check: 4 + 33 - 37 = 0, so P is on the line."
      ]
    },
